Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 17:52:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 067/154] test(atrium): unit-test the space filter and the
 claim ledger decision
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

atrium_browser_window.cc is 7905 lines and had no unit tests at all - only a
browsertest touched it, so every check on it needed a full browser and the VM.

Two extractions, chosen for logic where a wrong answer is silent rather than for
ease. ReopenRowsForActiveSpace lifts the space filter that RestoreSidebarSlice ran
inline; its JSON parsing was already tested but the filter that decides which rows
reopen was not, and that filter is the one that put tabs in the wrong space.
ClaimOwner, ApplyDetach and ApplyClaim lift the owner-versus-role comparison behind
the stale-detach and double-claim guards.

The claim mutation is the useful one: reverting ApplyDetach to compare full tags
rather than owners reproduces the exact regression logged three times before,
and the named test catches it.

No behaviour change. Deliberately left in place: OnSurfaceMessage's dispatch, the
AI panel's target resolution and ComputeAiRouteFacts - all need a live
TabStripModel or do real file I/O, so they are correctly browsertests. The settings
field readers are already pure but are thin lookups, not decisions, so extracting
them would only pad the count.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
